From e4b14be0df07ced9d60de54c0d55361a4020ed93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Solbjor <thomas.solbjor@fortedigital.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:56:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ask for a deployment prefix; tag resources with the deployer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The prefix was a hardcoded literal in every root module, yet it seeds
names that are globally unique across each provider (S3/GCS/object
buckets, the Cognito hosted-UI domain, Azure storage accounts and Key
Vaults) — two deployments on the defaults collided, and the only fix was
editing committed main.tf files.

- prefix is now a root-module variable set via terraform.tfvars, with
  validation (3-16 lowercase [a-z0-9-], no trailing dash; AWS also
  rejects aws/amazon/cognito, which Cognito bans in domains)
- Azure resource group derives as "<prefix>-rg"; AWS
  cognito_domain_prefix derives from the prefix — both TODOs gone
- prod default moves devhub -> devhub-prod for symmetry with dev
- new deployed_by variable, recorded on every resource as a
  DeployedBy tag (deployed-by label on GCP/UpCloud, sanitized to each
  provider's charset) alongside Deployment = prefix
- setup-env.sh asks for both: prefix with a per-tier default and the
  uniqueness explanation, deployer auto-detected from the cloud CLI
  (aws sts / az account / gcloud auth / UPCLOUD_USERNAME, falling back
  to user@host); new --prefix/--deployed-by flags, and --force re-runs
  prefill from the existing tfvars so a live deployment cannot be
  renamed by accident

terraform.tfvars is committed in generated environment repos, so both
values survive the GitOps handover.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
